WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:02.107
STEPHANIE WONG: This
week, we're talking

00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:04.632
about KubeCon, Cloud Run,
and querying ride share data.

00:00:04.632 --> 00:00:06.590
Welcome to "This Week in
Cloud," where we serve

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.690
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.190
Even if you didn't get a chance
to attend KubeCon this year,

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.232
you can still catch all
the biggest announcements

00:00:13.232 --> 00:00:16.070
in one place with this
KubeCon wrap-up post.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.170
Check out cool news like
monitoring Kubernetes

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.180
with Stackdriver
and see examples

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.450
of customers transforming their
industries with Kubernetes

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.780
all in one place.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:29.450
Read more and see how GKE
puts the "ease" in Kubernetes.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:31.130
We announced Cloud Run at Next.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.360
But that doesn't mean
we're done just yet.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.360
Check out all the
latest on the GCP Blog

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.790
to learn about some new
improvements to Cloud Run,

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.100
like Cloud SQL support
and metrics at a glance.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.580
You can also check out the
talk from Next for a deep dive

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.480
of how it works.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.140
So take a look and start getting
the most out of Cloud Run.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.240
As if BigQuery couldn't
already do enough,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.160
now you can get
insights even faster

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.520
thanks to BigQuery BI Engine.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.290
In a new post, developer
advocate Felipe Hoffa

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.570
built a BI dashboard
and explains

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.320
how to predict travel time based
on a location and time of day

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.660
with a public data
set from Uber.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.760
Try out Felipe's
dashboard for yourself

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.410
or get inspired to
see how BigQuery

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.020
can help you with your data.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.548
Of course, there's more than
BigQuery and Kubernetes in GCP.

00:01:15.548 --> 00:01:17.090
If you're still
exploring, then we've

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.250
got a playlist that
you're sure to enjoy--

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.710
Getting Started with
Google Cloud Platform.

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:24.230
This is a great set of
resources to learn some new tips

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.840
and get the basics on a
wide variety of topics,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:28.610
from setting up
roles to spinning off

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.367
compute and storage offerings.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.450
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:35.000
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.500
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.490
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.930
We'll see you in the cloud.

